	(text "100 Ω differential pairs; P on the transformer's - ends, N on its + ends, both sides (see the layout)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 189.23 201.93 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.85 0.85)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ea064e5f-4d06-f2db-8170-d43f705f29ca")
	)
	(text_box "+3V3_ETH is +3V3 through a ferrite bead (power sheet). The PHY address strap is the default (RXD3 pulled up internally): PHYAD = 1. No strap resistors on\nRXD0/RXD1: TXDLY = 0, RXDLY = 1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 330.2 335.28 0)
		(size 120.65 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f62451df-60ef-266c-2cf9-da5d2e69be2f")
	)
	(text_box "The FPGA talks RGMII (4-bit DDR at 125 MHz) at 3.3 V to the PHY; 22 Ω series resistors damp the lines. The PHY makes its own 1.0 V core with an internal switcher (REG_OUT, 2.2 µH). Straps on the LED pins are sampled at reset: CFG_EXT = 1 (external 3.3 V on DVDD_RG) and CFG_LDO[1:0] = 00 (3.3 V I/O pads), PHY address 1, TX delay off, RX delay on (the gateware's RGMII PHY expects the 2 ns\nreceive delay in the PHY and adds its own transmit delay). The magnetics are a G2406S module: each chip-side centre tap gets its own 100 nF to ground, as a voltage-mode driver wants; the line-side taps go to a Bob Smith termination (75 Ω each, 1 nF / 2 kV to ground)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 25.4 0)
		(size 340.36 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fedb86bf-910e-ef94-be58-73e17360988b")
	)
